  "chitchat": [
    "swirls something amber and watches the deep water with mild appetite.",
    "\"Everything down there's inventory. It simply doesn't know it yet.\""
  ],
  "description": "A platinum-tier shareholder in a suit that costs more than the building you were born in. He looks at the bay the way a cat looks at a fishbowl, and at you not at all. The building's staff call him Mr Brandt; he has never asked what they're called.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "He has already stopped seeing you."
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "...",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "The shareholder doesn't lower his glass. \"If you have to be up here, do try to be interesting. The last one wasn't.\" A pause, magnanimous. \"Brandt. Sinclair Brandt. You won't need it, but people find it settles them.\""
    }
